REFERENCE-ROOM CUTOVER PROOF — the Goals room, run as the real app_rw role
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Setup: local app_rw given a temporary LOGIN (reverted to NOLOGIN after), a
second app instance started with DATABASE_URL pointing at app_rw.
- /goals  (MIGRATED to withTenant): renders FULL data under app_rw — 2 active
  goals, named goals + pace. Real DB-level isolation is active and correct.
- /pipeline (NOT yet migrated): renders ALL ZEROS under app_rw ($0k, 0 opps,
  "No opportunities yet") — its bare getPool() queries hit RLS default-deny.
Conclusion: withTenant delivers real isolation under the non-owner role, and
unmigrated rooms FAIL CLOSED (empty, never cross-tenant). The flip is safe to
stage; every room must adopt withTenant before DATABASE_URL is pointed at app_rw.
resolve_user_org semantics fixed: uid null -> sole org; identified-but-
unprivileged uid -> NULL (no tenant), matching currentOrgId().

